<title>USA: Rauma Corp unit gets $50 mln Chilean order.</title>
<headline>Rauma Corp unit gets $50 mln Chilean order.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sunds Defibrator, a unit of Rauma Corp, said Wednesday that it has received an order from Chile's Industrial Forestales S Inforsa valued at $50 million.</p>
<p>The order is for a new thermomechanical pulp plant for newsprint that will be located south of Santiago, the company said.</p>
<p>Sunds said its units in Sweden, Finland and Chile will engineer and manufacture the equipment.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
